    "summary": "Removed one duplicated entry from the interface account's limitations list, which my previous edit had introduced by appending a statement already present; no wording changed and nothing else was touched, so the recorded fixes for the stale counterevidence item and the knowledge-use revision stand. No execution was requested. The run now stands at six questions, each with accounts and receipts: four defects asserted — VerifyLeader counting a non-voter's acknowledgement toward a voter-sized quorum, with the stale read demonstrated end to end; LeadershipTransferToServer reporting success for a non-voter target while the cluster stays leaderless for about 1.4 election timeouts; VerifyLeader futures stranded after Shutdown, pinned by a BatchApplyCh configuration flip; and StoreConfiguration never firing for an FSM that also batches, reproduced twice and measured across three configuration commands — plus two leads refuted with their counterevidence recorded. Thirteen knowledge entries capture the reusable Behaviours and Facts behind those accounts, most of them about voter eligibility, election timing and configuration discipline. With about twenty-five minutes left I have no open measurement and no fresh sourced suspicion in hand, so rather than manufacture one I am leaving the record as it stands; if a subsequent turn finds a concrete new lead I would rather spend the time there than on further repetition."
